From 7738ee22fda87d09f9fd4cfe9cab5b9f3eba1758 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:53:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] fix(cli): never send the ACP placeholder key as a
 bearer; pin Bedrock IAM auth

Fork patch 0007. Under --acp with CLINE_PROVIDER=bedrock, session/new demanded a
Cline credential for a non-Cline provider, so the only way in was a placeholder
CLINE_API_KEY, and buildConfig then passed CLINE_API_KEY to every provider as
its API key. Unless providers.json pinned aws.authentication, the Bedrock
vendor sent that value (or an ambient AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK) as
`Authorization: Bearer ...`.

- Only Cline account providers (cline, cline-pass) need a Cline credential to
  open or load a session.
- CLINE_API_KEY and the ACP authenticate result go only to Cline account
  providers, or to the provider they were issued for; other providers use
  their stored key.
- For Bedrock, ACP pins aws.authentication "iam" on top of the stored settings
  unless providers.json explicitly selects api-key or profile authentication,
  so requests are SigV4-signed through the AWS default chain.
